# Test: `ze doctor` reports an ethernet that overrides its MAC but binds by name.
#
# VALIDATES: the operator learns, from the command they already run, that
# `mac { address }` on a name-bound entry is written to whichever device holds
# that name. applyConfig (internal/component/iface/config_apply.go) calls
# SetMACAddress against the device the entry resolves to, on every apply, so a
# kernel rename hands one NIC's address to another.
# PREVENTS: the shape `ze init` wrote for every discovered NIC until 2026-09-02
# staying invisible on the boxes that already carry it.
#
# One command on purpose: reject=stdout:pattern= matches the whole file's
# accumulated stdout, so a second command printing the code would trip a reject
# in the sibling file. No exit-code assertion, because `ze doctor` reports on
# the whole machine and eth0 exists on no CI runner.

option=needs-linux

tmpfs=mac-override-by-name.conf:terminator=EOF_OVERRIDE
interface {
    backend netlink;
    ethernet eth0 {
        mac {
            address 02:00:00:00:00:01;
        }
    }
}
EOF_OVERRIDE

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze doctor --json mac-override-by-name.conf:timeout=60s
expect=stdout:contains=schema-version
expect=stdout:contains=doctor-iface-mac-override-by-name
